1
00:00:00,934 --> 00:00:01,954
(Leonard:)What?

2
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:05,965
(Raj:)Sheldon is a very smart man, and
he obviously wants to keep this a secret.

3
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:07,659
(Howard:)Yeah, so?

4
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:10,671
(Raj:)What if it's booby-trapped?

5
00:00:11,044 --> 00:00:13,704
(Howard:)Don't worry, I'm one step ahead of him.

6
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:16,250
Oh, great, what's your pl...?

7
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:23,015
(Howard:)Are we good?

8
00:00:23,490 --> 00:00:24,510
(Leonard:)Yeah.

9
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:32,995
(Raj:)Huh.

10
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,030
(Raj:)Forty-three.

11
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:37,673
(Raj:)What the hell does that mean?

12
00:00:37,838 --> 00:00:39,328
(Raj:)I don't know.

13
00:00:39,506 --> 00:00:42,876
(Howard:)- The solution to an equation?
- Maybe.

14
00:00:43,043 --> 00:00:44,913
(Raj:)It's a prime number.

15
00:00:45,078 --> 00:00:47,948
(Raj:)Encryption systems are built
on prime numbers.

16
00:00:48,115 --> 00:00:51,605
(Howard:)What kind of secret
does Sheldon have to encrypt?

17
00:00:51,785 --> 00:01:00,025
(Raj:)He's always been very cagey about what
he puts in his egg salad to make it so tasty.

